tsens_tz_sensor1 = 519   (51.9 C)     was 558 (55.8 C) when doc 72 started
tsens_tz_sensor8 = 535   (53.5 C)     was 580 (58.0 C)
pm8994_tz        = 45945 (45.9 C)     was 49125 (49.1 C)
battery          = 41200 (41.2 C)     was 42500 (42.5 C)
msm_therm        = 46    quiet_therm = 47
panel: alive, backlight 57..200 (driven by repowerd's own interface during this session)

===== 6. what an idle-ish device looks like now =====
busy 0.87 of 4 cores = 22%, idle 78%, iowait 0%, sys 15.0%
top kernel-side consumers by context switches per 10 s (host):
  rcu_preempt 7415 | ksoftirqd/2 3282 | rcu_sched 2795 | ksoftirqd/3 2560 | ksoftirqd/0 1869
  sensorfwd 1590 (372 of them involuntary) | ksoftirqd/1 1414 | kworker/u8:8 1281
  systemd-journald 695 | sensors@1.0-service 440 (78 threads)
  total 29244 context switches / 10 s across 602 tasks and 1587 threads.
  ie. ~83% of all context switches are the kernel's own (RCU, softirq, kworkers), and the only
  large userspace one is sensorfwd + the sensors HAL -- the doc-71 pair. There is no single
  runaway userspace process left to blame for the rest.
